<title>JAPAN: Japan reports &quot;medium&quot; earthquake.</title>
<headline>Japan reports &quot;medium&quot; earthquake.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A &quot;medium earthquake&quot;, about 100 km (60 miles) northeast of Tokyo, shook the Japanese capital on Sunday, meteorological authorities reported.</p>
<p>The epicentre was in Ibaragi prefecture.</p>
<p>In a statement, Japan's Meteorological Agency said the quake was measured some 70 km (45 miles) under the earth.</p>
<p>An agency spokesman said there were no dangers of a so-called Tsunami or tidal wave.</p>
<p>&quot;It was a medium shake,&quot; an agency spokesman told Reuters.</p>
</text>
